WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
- Buckle up folks.

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:02.750
This is gonna be a rough one.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.540
I've never gotten to as
many Twitter arguments

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.390
as I have in the last week.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.050
I cannot believe what's going on.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.430
There is hypocrisy, there's inaccuracy,

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.780
degrading information

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.180
from respected journalists and physicians.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.810
But I think we should
start with President Trump

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.400
being diagnosed and dealing with COVID-19.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.720
The way I actually found out

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.170
about President Trump's diagnosis was

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.910
that I was woken up three
or four or even five times

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.030
in the middle of the night
by TV producers and stations

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.580
asking me to come on to talk
about the president's health.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.300
But when I investigated further,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.270
the only thing we knew at that moment was

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.670
that president Trump tweeted
that he tested positive

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.160
for COVID-19 along with the First Lady.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.930
Here's the problem with
going on television

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.080
without any information,
you're bound to speculate.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.570
And when you're speculating,

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.340
you're practicing what's
known as tabloid medicine.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.230
This is a very inaccurate
and unethical way

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.430
to talk about health.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.930
You're really speculating
about a patient's health,

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.520
who is not your patient

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.000
and someone who hasn't given
you explicit permission

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.280
to talk about their health.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.250
So not only are you doing
something unethical,

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.580
it's also gonna be inaccurate
'cause you're guessing

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.950
and I did not wanna be guessing

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.780
so I turned down those opportunities,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.150
even though I love talking about COVID-19

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.080
and putting accurate
information out there.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.970
To my dismay, I saw
conversations the next day

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.440
in the media that went as such.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.550
- Dr. Batocera what do
you see in that video?

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.790
Does that give us any sense
of the president's condition

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:29.970
or does he look okay?

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.600
Some people thought he
looked a little pale.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.550
- Something that also upset me that day

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.680
was seeing med Twitter

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.730
for my fellow physician colleagues explode

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.550
with negative commentary,

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:43.600
wishing that Trump passes from COVID-19,

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.490
wishing harm or demise to him,

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:48.660
which goes against every
medical rule in the book.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.060
When we took our oath,

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.830
it was to first do no harm
and provide the best care

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.730
to every patient, irrespective

00:01:55.730 --> 00:02:00.560
to geography, race, criminal
status, political biases.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.890
So to see doctors say

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.400
that some patients shouldn't
get better is just awful.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.580
I was incredibly proud of
Vice President Joe Biden

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.550
coming out and saying that
he wishes President Trump

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:11.800
a speedy recovery,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.380
that they don't wanna bad
mouth him in this given moment.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.560
That is the right thing to do.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.020
And I believe my fellow
physician colleagues

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.110
should be leading the way in that charge.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.200
Now let's move on and
talk about what's going on

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.340
from Trump's organization standpoint,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.120
the way that they're handling
COVID-related messaging

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.890
and the messaging about
president Trump's health.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.360
Honestly, it's horrible.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.070
It's impossible to know whether
they're telling the truth,

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.480
if they're simply confused, if
they're getting facts wrong.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.850
I've actually seen president
Trump's personal doctor

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.110
come out and make questionable statements

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.340
where I can't even follow the story.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.500
Did he get oxygen?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.790
Did he not get oxygen?

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.880
What were the medications
that he was given?

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.410
When were the medications given?

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.320
The timeline is all over the place

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.540
and it's difficult to tell what's what.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.270
This list of all the
medications and supplements

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.790
that President Trump has
received make no sense to me

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.150
from a scientific standpoint.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.260
Many of these treatments are under

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.220
an emergency use authorization

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.430
where it should be reserved
for those who are most ill.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.250
Those who have no alternative
means of getting better,

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.870
because they're not proven.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.480
They haven't been FDA approved.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.420
And yet president Trump got all of them.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.040
Either the president was
more ill than they let on,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.490
or the president was getting

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.350
a lot of treatments prematurely.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.010
And this point is what really
gets me the most upset.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.780
It really functions as the worst example

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:36.320
of how media has become
more gossip than journalism,

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.920
where you're valuing
popularity on Twitter,

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.870
over journalistic integrity and accuracy.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.070
And I'm specifically talking
about the negative labeling

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.410
of the president's personal physician,

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.580
being a doctor of
osteopathic medicine, a DO.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.490
Folks, there are two types
of practicing physicians here

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.910
in the United States, MDs and DOs.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.130
They both go through four
years of medical school.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.130
They then go into a residency program

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.250
where they become specialized
in their training.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.050
In fact, now that the
residency programs have merged,

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.800
DOs and MDs train side by side.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.820
They oftentimes take the
exact same board exams,

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:14.400
the same licensing exams in
order to practice medicine.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.390
The fact that we have
some journalists tweeting

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.320
that the president's
doctor is bad or wrong

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:26.320
or a worse doctor because
of his degree is shameful

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.230
and horribly inaccurate.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.930
The one that I took
exception to the most was

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:33.587
by a screenwriter by the
name of Eric Haywood.

00:04:33.587 --> 00:04:36.007
"Look, I'm sure, checks notes,

00:04:36.007 --> 00:04:38.917
"doctor of osteopathic
medicine is a fine achievement

00:04:38.917 --> 00:04:41.337
"and Dr. Conley had to study super hard

00:04:41.337 --> 00:04:43.997
"to earn his, uh, certificate, degree.

00:04:43.997 --> 00:04:45.207
"I don't know, man, whatever."

00:04:45.207 --> 00:04:46.757
"Your little president is being treated

00:04:46.757 --> 00:04:50.337
"by someone a couple notches
higher than an acupuncturist.

00:04:50.337 --> 00:04:51.750
"Sorry to this country."

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:52.583
What?

00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:55.470
As an individual who frequently advocates

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.810
to have decreased discrimination

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.680
and stereotyping in this nation,

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.030
you are doing just that, sir.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.270
And on top of it,

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.710
you're mad at Trump's administration

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.040
for spreading potential misinformation.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.110
You are doing just that!

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:14.490
DOs are just as equally licensed
to practice medicine here

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.120
in the United States and
in 50 countries abroad.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.830
In fact, there's over 120,000
practicing DOs out there,

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.350
and God forbid you end
up in an emergency room

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.700
or in a trauma situation.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.880
I'm sure you're not gonna be checking

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.460
if there's a DO or MD saving your life.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.460
You're gonna trust that this
doctor, whoever they may be,

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:34.990
will be acting in good conscience

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.320
to save your life despite
your nasty comments above.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.580
And I have to give a huge
thank you to my MD colleagues

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.500
who jumped at the defense

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.540
of doctors of osteopathic medicine.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.070
Those who tweeted in support,

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.720
explaining that we work side by side,

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:52.730
many times not knowing
who's an MD and who's a DO.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:56.260
Before I used to think
that these types of tweets

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.810
were largely coming from institutions

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.160
that perhaps didn't have the
highest journalistic integrity.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.280
And then I saw a tweet by Ryan Lizza,

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:07.350
the chief Washington
correspondent from Politico

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:09.777
and a senior political analyst at CNN.

00:06:09.777 --> 00:06:11.550
"D.O. Twitter,"

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.090
which by the way, is med Twitter

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.017
because Dos and MDs are both doctors.

00:06:15.017 --> 00:06:16.747
"Is mad at me for pointing out

00:06:16.747 --> 00:06:18.857
"that Conley is not an MD,

00:06:18.857 --> 00:06:21.530
"but they are clearly
not sending their best!"

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.960
I don't know what journalist who works

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:27.000
for these legitimate
companies has the gall

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:32.000
in the midst of a pandemic
where over 120,000 doctors

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.350
are acting as frontline healthcare workers

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.540
to say that we're not sending our best.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.210
Osteopathic physicians died

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.550
while you write articles at home.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:45.320
How dare you attack these doctors?

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.670
These are women and
men putting their lives

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:48.680
on the front lines.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.150
If a nurse said something you didn't like,

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:55.450
would you say nurses
aren't sending their best?

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:58.300
The fact that you feel
comfortable putting this out there

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:01.480
and not deleting it after you
get negative feedback for it

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.910
speaks volumes about the
lack of caring you put

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:06.440
in the accuracy of your tweets.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.880
We should not be judging doctors

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.890
based on the letters after their name,

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.210
but instead judging them
by their bedside manner,

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.480
their ability to heal patients,

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:17.450
their ability to fight misinformation

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.040
and their ability to
connect to other humans.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.280
And a little fun fact for Ryan here,

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:26.200
Vice President Biden's personal
physician is also a DO.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.250
So clearly we are sending our best

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.370
or is it only our best when it suits you?

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.667
Here's Christina Farr's tweet.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.407
"I'm disturbed that anyone,

00:07:34.407 --> 00:07:36.587
"let alone 13% of Americans,

00:07:36.587 --> 00:07:40.407
"say the most important way
they get their news is YouTube.

00:07:40.407 --> 00:07:43.870
"No wonder belief in conspiracy
theories is so prevalent."

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.007
I had a lot of problems
with this so I responded.

00:07:46.007 --> 00:07:49.147
"Not only do major news
organizations post a ton of content

00:07:49.147 --> 00:07:51.507
"on YouTube, but so do
legitimate medical sources

00:07:51.507 --> 00:07:55.097
"like the CDC, WHO, and individual doctors

00:07:55.097 --> 00:07:58.397
"like MamaDoctorJones,
Medlife Crisis, &amp; myself.

00:07:58.397 --> 00:08:01.127
"I would also venture to
say that mainstream media

00:08:01.127 --> 00:08:04.320
"has done less than an ideal
job covering COVID-19 anyway."

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.710
The reason I say this is

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.980
because I have several videos,
fact checking the media

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.657
in their coverage of COVID-19.

00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:12.997
"I'm not saying there
isn't good info on YouTube.

00:08:12.997 --> 00:08:15.647
"I'd instead suggest
that it's highly variable

00:08:15.647 --> 00:08:18.447
"and often times can be extreme
and polarizing in nature.

00:08:18.447 --> 00:08:20.607
"Information gleaned from
traditional news outlets

00:08:20.607 --> 00:08:21.507
"is not the same.

00:08:21.507 --> 00:08:23.147
"There are checks and balances,

00:08:23.147 --> 00:08:25.340
"as well as editorial oversight."

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.190
I don't understand because
if I watch CNN and Fox news,

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.300
it looks like I'm living
in two different countries.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.790
The points of views don't align at all.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:35.680
So there's a huge variability
even on television.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.770
Mainstream media has taken
this extremist approach

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.320
where you don't know what you're getting,

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.880
and there's huge variability
in mainstream media as well.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.660
So to critique people
getting their information

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.690
on YouTube is unfair.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.830
When we see how much
journalistic integrity

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.750
has been degraded in this country,

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:57.750
I think it's fair that certain
will trust MamaDoctorJones

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.120
before they trust One America News.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.800
We should not judge people for that.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:05.690
I think President Trump
certainly acted inappropriately

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:10.450
when he decided to take a
cruise in his armored SUV

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.280
in the midst of his stay in the hospital.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:15.460
We have enough difficulties
keeping patients safe

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.200
and staff safe when it comes to COVID-19.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.060
Making these unnecessary motions

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:22.090
just put a lot of lives at risk.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.810
But at the same time, I strongly disagree.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:27.867
Vehemently disagree, if you
will, with tweets like this.

00:09:27.867 --> 00:09:30.737
"Congress might want
to defund Walter Reed.

00:09:30.737 --> 00:09:32.700
"It is a public health hazard."

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.650
This is written by an MSNBC contributor

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:37.580
and Washington Post columnist,

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:41.180
trying to encourage defunding
of a veteran's hospital

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.910
because she didn't like

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.460
how they handled the
President Trump situation.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:49.430
Our anger towards our political foes

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.380
has gone so far that we're willing

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.480
to let people lose their lives

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.290
because we disagree with them.

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:58.210
When did the disagreement become this bad

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.070
that you're willing to allow bystanders

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.310
to get hurt in this process.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.520
To hurt veterans

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.620
because you don't like the
way something was handled.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.680
There's better ways to speak up

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.000
and I think the only
thing these messages do

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.930
is improve Twitter
followings and like counts

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:13.020
'cause they're so extremist.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.510
You're not bringing people together.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.050
You're not improving the world.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.530
This type of rhetoric should be shut down

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.050
and I'm not saying shut down by Twitter,

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.510
it should be shut down by you and I.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.730
In the midst of filming this video,

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.070
President Trump actually
put out a message saying

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:28.540
that we shouldn't be afraid of
COVID-19, that he dominated.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.800
We're all gonna beat it.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.540
Well, President Trump, if
we're being honest here

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.570
over 200,000 Americans have
lost their lives to it,

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.403
who didn't beat it.

00:10:35.403 --> 00:10:38.260
So to downplay like this
is inaccurate and unfair.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:40.360
There are things we can
empower ourselves with.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.942
We should be alert up to
date as best as we can be

00:10:42.942 --> 00:10:44.730
so we can make it the best decisions

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:45.880
for ourselves and our families.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:46.760
It's pretty incredible,

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:49.117
but the stay alert, not anxious mantra

00:10:49.117 --> 00:10:52.990
has really held up from
day one of this pandemic,

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:54.570
but the message of don't be afraid,

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.930
we'll all beat it and we'll
all dominate is not true.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.950
Many people will continue
to lose their lives.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.010
So we need to be smart.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.220
We need to wear masks.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.640
We need to socially distance.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.560
The fall season is upon us
and things can get really bad

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.810
if there is a second wave.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.375
We're more prepared than we were before.

00:11:08.375 --> 00:11:10.820
We are actually making major adjustments

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:11.970
in our medical institutions

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.720
in terms of treatments,
care, additional units,

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.990
staffing, personal protective equipment.

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.920
So we are gonna fare better than we did

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.590
in the beginning of this pandemic.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.710
But that doesn't mean that it's a joke

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.210
and we shouldn't take it seriously.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:27.320
The 1 million death mark
recently was just passed

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:28.700
with COVID-19 worldwide.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.927
That's a somber reminder of
how serious this virus is.

00:11:31.927 --> 00:11:34.360
And the last thing I urge
everyone at home to do

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.280
is get your flu shots

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.950
because when there's
already tremendous pressure

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:39.830
on the hospitals,

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:42.690
we wanna make sure as
few people as possible

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.470
are getting sick with flu, especially

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.100
because we have a vaccine that is safe,

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.620
that almost everyone
universally should be getting.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.490
In fact, I just got mine the other day

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:52.530
and I'm gonna highlight it

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:55.110
for you on one of my hospital blog videos.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:57.360
But for now I want you
to check out my other day

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.230
in the life video here in the hospital

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.820
as an osteopathic physician,

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:05.350
or check out me debunking more
myths about COVID-19 here.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.844
As always stay happy and healthy.

00:12:07.844 --> 00:12:10.427
(upbeat music)

